<title>JAPAN: British Columbia launches 4.90% yen/dlr samurai.</title>
<headline>British Columbia launches 4.90% yen/dlr samurai.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/dollar dual-currency samurai issue was announced by lead manager Yamaichi Securities on Wednesday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Province of British Columbia</p>
<p> AMT		 70 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    4.90 pct</p>
<p> MATURITY	  29 Feb 2000</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  28 Feb 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	Feb 17 to Feb 27</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Semi-annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AA+, Moody's Aa2</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Yamaichi Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    Industrial Bank of Japan</p>
<p>NOTE: Holders of the samurai bonds will receive $4,029.01 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity. -- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
